      "notes": "Verdict is well-reasoned and appropriately cautious. The 'negligible' direction with 'minor' magnitude and 'low' confidence correctly reflects that broadband infrastructure has no direct education mechanism. Claim tiers are appropriate: E17 is labelled measurable but is actually a general assertion from governmentbusiness.co.uk (a media source); however, it is used only to support a soft, hedged claim and does not drive the verdict. E24 from futurescot.com is labelled measurable \u2014 this is a borderline case as it describes an ongoing situation rather than a projection, acceptable here. The magnitude/time_horizon pairing is technically inconsistent with schema rules only if direction were 'too-uncertain' (it is not), so 'minor'/'long-term' with 'negligible' direction is permissible. No party identity leakage, no lever scoring, no false balance issues detected."
